    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so in the AC one, because it's constantly charging and discharging, does that mean the capacitor isn't actually \"blocking\" the current like it does in DC? it feels like there's some kind of constant movement happening even though the plates aren't physically touching. can u explain the mechanism behind that a bit more?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
