      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are spot on; the current flow in AC is a continuous oscillation of charge movement across the insulating dielectric. The current doesn't truly \"flow\" through the capacitor in the traditional sense, as the dielectric prevents direct conduction. Instead, the changing voltage drives a displacement current as charge accumulates on the plates, perfectly opposing the voltage change.",
